Built a Monte Carlo simulation model running over 6000 simulations to estimate NBA championship probabilities. Model runs off of a team strength rating system combining pace, scoring metrics, point differential, clutch performance, injuries, age, and playoff experience. Full playoff bracket setup including play-in tournament, the % chance of each team represents how often they won in each simulation.

Model originally created for the 2024-2025 playoffs but continuosly updating data and tweaking the model from season to season to improve accuracy. 

